.TH CYAML_CREATE_DICTIONARY_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_create_dictionary_mp, cyaml_create_dictionary \- allocate an empty YAML dictionary node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_create_dictionary_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
cyaml cyaml_create_dictionary(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocate a DOM node of type CYAML_DICTIONARY.  A chashmap holds its
entries (separate chaining, string->pointer).  The dictionary is empty at
first.  Add children to it with cyaml_dictionary_set().
cyaml_create_dictionary() passes NULL for mp.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mp   Custom allocator, or NULL for default.
     The library keeps its own copy of the struct, so the caller may
     release or reuse the struct once this call returns. The functions
     that it names must stay callable until the last node built with
     them is destroyed. A process can use at most 64 distinct sets of
     four functions; a call that would need a 65th fails and returns
     NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New cyaml node on success, NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_dictionary_set (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_size (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
